From f931844f77e9e70504562f00a021e87b142959da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:34:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 46/50] cellGcmSys: no emergency recycle of a ring the
 runtime's callback owns

The drain recycles a title's ring itself when the title's buffer-full
callback seems not to, judged by `current >= end`. But `current` sits
exactly at `end` whenever a title fills the ring to the byte, until its
next reserve calls the callback -- and when that callback is the
runtime's own (cellGcm_fifo_recycle), it does recycle. Recycling under it
rewound the ring beneath the title: 3D Dot Game Heroes stalled 3.4 s
crossing into another field area.

Now a ring whose callback is the runtime's is left to it, and only
`current > end` counts as an overrun. The same crossing: 58.4 fps, with
only the game's own 1.3 s load.
---
 libs/video/cellGcmSys.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index b0c7201..0125c44 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -3013,7 +3013,15 @@ static void gcm_rsx_process_fifo_unlocked(void)
         /* `end` is the walker's position, not the ring's: being near it is the
          * title catching up with the walker, which its callback handles. */
         else if (s_ring_limit_end) head_consumed = 0;
-        else if (begin && end > begin && cur >= end) { head_consumed = 1; s_title_overran = 1; }
+        /* A ring whose callback is the runtime's own is recycled by it
+         * (cellGcm_fifo_recycle), and `current` AT `end` is no overrun: the
+         * reserve calls the callback only when current + n > end, so a title
+         * that fills the ring exactly sits there until its next reserve. 3D
+         * Dot Game Heroes does, and recycling it then rewound the ring under
+         * it: a 3.4 s stall crossing into another field area. */
+        else if (vm_read32(ctx + 0xC) && vm_read32(vm_read32(ctx + 0xC)) == GCM_FIFO_CALLBACK_SENTINEL_EA)
+            head_consumed = 0;
+        else if (begin && end > begin && cur > end) { head_consumed = 1; s_title_overran = 1; }
         if (begin && end > begin && cur >= begin && cur + GCM_RECYCLE_SLACK >= end
                 && head_consumed && s_title_overran) {
             u32 io_begin = gcm_ea2io(begin);
